{
  "case_id": "2006-05-1541",
  "document_hash": "6be202812f376528a2c36f12d2d704676486ec390f225f217a9eb36b47d6481f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1541",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6be202812f376528a2c36f12d2d704676486ec390f225f217a9eb36b47d6481f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6be202812f37-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Defendant, in unequivocal language of section 1346, waives sovereign immunity and permits a refund suit by a third party such as Petitioner. That conclusion that I've stated to the Court was supported by the holding in United States versus Williams."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1541",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6be202812f376528a2c36f12d2d704676486ec390f225f217a9eb36b47d6481f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6be202812f37-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: And why did the court point out twice in Williams that section 7426 was not available?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1541",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6be202812f376528a2c36f12d2d704676486ec390f225f217a9eb36b47d6481f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6be202812f37-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: You're not challenging the amount of the assessed tax, are you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1541",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6be202812f376528a2c36f12d2d704676486ec390f225f217a9eb36b47d6481f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6be202812f37-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Government contended that Mrs. Williams had remedies available to her, certainly not a levy, because there was no levy, but the Government was contending she could have sought relief under the Quiet Title Act. She could have sought relief by posting --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1541",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6be202812f376528a2c36f12d2d704676486ec390f225f217a9eb36b47d6481f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6be202812f37-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: You want to say no to that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Maynard",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1541",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6be202812f376528a2c36f12d2d704676486ec390f225f217a9eb36b47d6481f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6be202812f37-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When Congress creates a specific remedy for a specific situation that remedy forecloses resort to a more general remedy when that general remedy would frustrate the purposes of the specific remedy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1541",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6be202812f376528a2c36f12d2d704676486ec390f225f217a9eb36b47d6481f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6be202812f37-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Was, was the more specific statute there enacted after the more general statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1541",
      "confidence": 0.0,
